  "id": "COMPOUND:19839 - PROTEIN:3049",
  "verbalization": "Macrosporin is implicated in the regulation of Cytochrome c4 through a series of molecular interactions involving G1/S-specific cyclin-D1. The evidence suggests that Macrosporin acts as a target for multiple compounds, all of which ultimately target Cytochrome c4. These compounds—G1/S-specific cyclin-D1, 6-O-Acetyldihydrohelenalin, and 5-O-Demethylpaxanthonin—indirectly influence Cytochrome c4 by modulating the expression or activity of their target. The shared pathway from Macrosporin to G1/S-specific cyclin-D1 and then to Cytochrome c4 indicates a potential mechanism where Macrosporin may regulate the expression of these cyclin-D1 isoforms, which in turn affect Cytochrome c4 activity. The final score of 0.6177 in path_80498 and 0.6157 in paths_80499 and 80500 suggests a consistent and plausible mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction between Macrosporin and G1/S-specific cyclin-D1 remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a role for Macrosporin in modulating the expression of cyclin-D1, which may influence Cytochrome c4 activity, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm this relationship.",
